00:56:19.400 --> 00:56:23.340
Reed, if you were to say what the source
of your success as a leader is,

00:56:23.340 --> 00:56:24.010
what would you say?

00:56:26.230 --> 00:56:29.690
&gt;&gt; I'm always interested in kind of core
fundamental principles.

00:56:29.690 --> 00:56:34.480
And I've had a good ability to not get
distracted by transitory things.

00:56:34.480 --> 00:56:36.390
You know?
How you're supposed to be

00:56:36.390 --> 00:56:41.050
as opposed to just being able to be myself
and the company to be able to be itself.

00:56:41.050 --> 00:56:46.310
And, so there's a, a very strong sense of
groundedness as opposed to, let's

00:56:46.310 --> 00:56:49.570
figure out what other people are doing or
follow the fad or that kind of thing.

00:56:49.570 --> 00:56:51.320
So that gets you through a lot.

00:56:51.320 --> 00:56:52.320
You know?
If you sort of

00:56:52.320 --> 00:56:56.680
stick to the fundamentals,um, and are, are
pretty good at,

00:56:56.680 --> 00:57:03.770
trying to avoid, well both distraction
and, you know, false profits.

00:57:03.770 --> 00:57:04.690
&gt;&gt; That's fantastic.

00:57:04.690 --> 00:57:09.145
Let me, let me end by asking you to
recommend one TV show to the audience.

